; Division by zero is a reported runtime failure — not a silent drop, and
; not a NaN or an infinity. Both `/` and `mod` guard it, and both surface
; as `expr_type_mismatch`: the bucket `Host.evalExpr` has mapped
; `DivisionByZero` into since it was written, reused here rather than
; appending a new wire code for a case the message already names exactly
; ("division by zero while evaluating `(/ …)`").
;
; Form 2 is the surviving neighbour. Two failures cost two results, not
; the run — the same property `expr-value-interpolation` pins for an
; inverted `clamp` range.
(/ 1.0 0.0)
(mod 1.0 0.0)
(/ 10.0 4.0)
